.SS "server.listeners[].tcp.yara"
.PP
YARA rules over the bytes a layer 4 listener relays. The engine is a subset of the language implemented in Go \[u2014] this proxy links no C library into the data plane, and \fBCGO_ENABLED=0\fR is a property worth more here than the last few features of the grammar. What is supported:
.RS 3n
.PP
.ti -3n
\(bu
\fBstrings\fR: text with \fBnocase\fR, \fBwide\fR, \fBascii\fR, \fBfullword\fR and \fBprivate\fR; hex with \fB??\fR and \fB4?\fR wildcards and \fB[n]\fR or \fB[n\-m]\fR jumps; regular expressions (RE2, with the \fBi\fR and \fBs\fR flags).
.PP
.ti -3n
\(bu
\fBconditions\fR: \fB$a\fR, \fBnot\fR, \fBand\fR, \fBor\fR, parentheses, \fBN of them\fR, \fBany of them\fR, \fBall of them\fR, \fBN of ($a*)\fR, \fB#a\fR and \fBfilesize\fR compared with a number, \fBtrue\fR, \fBfalse\fR.
.PP
.ti -3n
\(bu
\fBnot supported\fR: modules and \fBimport\fR, \fBat\fR, \fBin\fR, \fBfor\fR loops, \fBentrypoint\fR, unbounded jumps (\fB[2\-]\fR), alternation inside a hex string, string offsets and lengths (\fB@a\fR, \fB!a\fR), and the \fBxor\fR and \fBbase64\fR modifiers.
.RE
.PP
.PP
Anything outside that is \fBrefused at load\fR, with the line number. A rule that silently matched nothing would be worse than one that will not start.
.PP
Two things differ from scanning a file, and both are deliberate. A rule is reported the first time its condition becomes true, not at the end: a decision that arrives after the last byte is a decision about a transfer that already happened. And \fBfilesize\fR means the bytes seen so far, which is the only honest reading when there is no end yet.
.PP
.TS
