.SS "upstreams[].canary"
.PP
A canary release inside one pool: the endpoints marked \fBcanary: true\fR receive the requests the policy selects and no others, so a new version can be exercised by testers (a header or a cookie), then by a share of everyone (\fBpercent\fR), then promoted by marking the old endpoints out. Selected requests fall back to the ordinary endpoints when no canary is available, and ordinary requests fall back to the canaries when the rest is down, unless \fBfallback: false\fR. Session affinity and hashing apply within the chosen side. \fBcanary: true\fR in the access log marks responses from a canary endpoint; \fBGET /v1/pools\fR counts canary requests and fallbacks. For a canary on a separate pool selected by header, use \fBroutes[].headers\fR instead.
.PP
.TS
