.SS "upstreams[].circuit_breaker"
.PP
Outlier ejection removes one failing endpoint from a healthy pool; the circuit breaker stops sending to a pool that fails as a whole and probes it back. Closed, it counts consecutive failed attempts across the pool (connection errors, timeouts, 503 and \fBretry_on\fR statuses; a success resets the count). At \fBconsecutive_failures\fR it opens: every request is refused at once with 503 and \fBRetry\-After\fR set to the remaining open time, without touching the upstream, for \fBopen_for\fR times the number of consecutive reopens (capped at ten). Then it is half open: \fBhalf_open_requests\fR trials may be in flight, a success closes the circuit and resets the back\-off, a failure reopens it. \fBxproxyctl upstreams\fR and \fBGET /v1/pools\fR show the state, the count, opens and refusals; \fBxproxy_upstream_circuit_state\fR and \fBxproxy_upstream_circuit_open_total\fR export them; refusals appear in the access log with \fBupstream_error: circuit_open\fR.
.PP
