.SS "Kind \fByara\fR"
.PP
The same engine as a tcp listener\(aqs \fByara\fR section, over request and response bodies. The supported subset and the reasons for it are described under \fBserver.listeners[].tcp.yara\fR.
.PP
The difference is that a body is buffered to \fBmax_bytes\fR before it is forwarded, so a match can refuse the request rather than only record it. A body larger than the bound is scanned to the bound and then streamed on \[u2014] holding an arbitrary upload in memory is a worse failure than an unscanned tail \[u2014] and the access log marks those with \fByara_partial\fR.
.PP
.TS
