.SS "Kind \fBldap_auth\fR"
.PP
HTTP Basic authentication against an LDAP or Active Directory server. Two modes: a \fBdirect bind\fR substitutes the username into \fBbind_dn_template\fR and binds with the password; a \fBsearch then bind\fR binds an optional service account (\fBbind_dn\fR), searches \fBbase_dn\fR with \fBuser_filter\fR for the user\(aqs entry, then binds as that entry, optionally requiring group membership. The username is escaped (RFC 4514 for a DN, RFC 4515 for a filter) so it cannot alter the query. \fBldaps://\fR and \fBstart_tls\fR verify the server certificate against the system roots or \fBca_file\fR. Verified credentials are cached by digest for \fBcache_ttl\fR; a directory or network error is never cached and denies the request.
.PP
