The hidden field is the classic: an input the stylesheet hides and \fBautocomplete="off"\fR keeps a password manager out of, with a name worth filling in (\fBcontact_reason\fR, \fBwebsite\fR). A person never sees it, so a value in it is a signal with no false positive to trade away \[u2014] unlike timing, which is why \fBfields\fR is the option to reach for first.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
.ft CR
<div style="position:absolute;left:\-9999px" aria\-hidden="true">
  <label>Leave this empty<input type="text" name="contact_reason"
         tabindex="\-1" autocomplete="off"></label>
