T}	T{
list of CIDR
T}	T{
The client address
T}
T{
\fBnot_\:subjects\fR,\: \fBnot_\:groups\fR,\: \fBnot_\:networks\fR
T}	T{
list
T}	T{
"Everybody but". Separate keys rather than a \fB!\fR prefix,\: because a group name can begin with anything
T}
.TE
.PP
Every selector a rule names has to hold. A rule that names none matches everything: as a deny that is a legitimate backstop, and as an allow it is a policy that says yes to everything, so it fails the load \[u2014] write \fBdefault: allow\fR if that is what is meant.
.PP
The first matching rule decides, so a deny above an allow carves an exception out of it:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
.ft CR
rules:
  \- {name: no\-deletes\-from\-the\-field, allow: false, methods: [DELETE], not_networks: ["10.0.0.0/8"]}
  \- {name: staff, allow: true, groups: ["cn=staff,ou=groups,dc=example,dc=com"]}
.ft
.fi
.RE
.PP
A refusal tells the client nothing about why: which rule, which group it would have needed, and whether the path even exists are all things a prober would like to know. The reason is in the proxy\(aqs own log and the access line carries \fBauthz_rule\fR, which is the only way to tell a policy that allowed from one that never matched.
.PP
\fBWhat feeds it.\fR \fBoidc\fR records the groups from \fBgroups_claim\fR (default \fBgroups\fR), the scopes from the token\(aqs \fBscope\fR, and whatever \fBattr_claims\fR names; \fBldap_auth\fR records the directory\(aqs own groups from \fBgroup_attr\fR; \fBapi_key\fR records the key\(aqs scopes. A filter that records nothing still records the subject, so \fBsubjects\fR and \fBkinds\fR work everywhere.
.SS "Kind \fBgrpc_guard\fR"
.PP
Reads gRPC messages rather than passing them through. A proxy that routes gRPC by its path has read the envelope; the messages are length\-prefixed frames of protobuf inside the body, and without reading them it cannot say how large one message is (only how large the whole body is), cannot notice a stream that stops in the middle of a frame, and cannot see a message nested a thousand deep \[u2014] which costs the backend\(aqs parser far more than it costs the sender to write.
.PP
No schema is used, deliberately. A schema has to be kept in step with the service, and a check that is only as current as its schema is a check that quietly stops applying the week somebody adds a field. The protobuf wire format carries the field number and the wire type, which is enough for every bound here.
.PP
.TS
