.SS "routes[].policy"
.PP
The route\(aqs positive security model: what a request may look like. Everything outside it is refused right after route matching, before virtual patches\(aq successors (rate limits, filters, the WAF) spend work on the request, with a terse status, reason \fBpolicy\fR and a \fBdetail\fR attribute in the security event naming the check (\fBmethod:DELETE\fR, \fBcontent_type:application/xml\fR, \fBquery:id:not_int\fR, \fBheader_count:41\fR and so on). Refusals count in \fBdenied_policy\fR and feed ban triggers under \fBpolicy\fR. \fBroutes[].methods\fR selects the route; \fBpolicy.methods\fR refuses, with 405 and an \fBAllow\fR header.
.PP
